-- title:
--   Prime-to-p level raising is finite étale on the j-finite chart
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M\ge 5$ with $p\nmid M$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{p\}$, let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity, and let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $L$ as its fraction field such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ lies in the image of $A\to L$. Let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell\nmid M p$. Let $K_M$ and $K_N$ be intermediate fields of the Laurent series field $L((q))$ over $L$, equal respectively to the $L$-subfield of $L((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(M)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and of that of $\Gamma_1(M\ell)$, each carrying an $A$-algebra structure compatible with $A\to L$. Let $j_M\in K_M$ and $j_N\in K_N$ have as underlying Laurent series the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant, both assumed nonzero, and assume $K_M\le K_N$. Let $\iota_M$ be an $A$-algebra homomorphism from the subalgebra of elements of $K_M$ integral over $A[j_M]$ to the subalgebra of elements of $K_N$ integral over $A[j_N]$, which is compatible with the inclusions of both fields into $L((q))$ (so $\iota_M$ is the restriction of the inclusion $K_M\subseteq K_N$). Then the underlying ring homomorphism of $\iota_M$ is finite and étale.
--
--   This is the good-reduction input for raising the level by a prime $\ell$ prime to $Mp$: on the $j$-finite affine chart of the two-chart integral model over the discrete valuation ring $A$ above $p$ in $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_p)$, the map of normalisations of $A[j]$ induced by $X_1(M\ell)\to X_1(M)$ is finite and étale, generic fibre included. It is used by the statements that exhibit the corresponding map at level $Mp$ as a base change, and in particular by the pushout statement for the chart algebras of $X_1(M\ell p)$ over those of $X_1(Mp)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_XOne_finite_and_etale_chartAlgFin_levelRaise_x1.lean

